01:18:45.280 --> 01:18:47.120
Even worse is the fact that the virus

01:18:47.120 --> 01:18:49.100
hasn't simply infected those memories

01:18:49.100 --> 01:18:52.200
that HOBA accessed in person in the HOS program.

01:18:52.200 --> 01:18:54.540
Every computer memory that's come into contact

01:18:54.540 --> 01:18:58.040
with a Hyper-O system associated program is also infected.

01:18:58.040 --> 01:18:59.800
That means it goes on spreading.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.960
They're working to try to produce an effective vaccine against the virus,

01:19:03.060 --> 01:19:05.420
only the trouble is it's complex and there isn't much time.

01:19:05.660 --> 01:19:09.440
Well, it would have been an advantage to be told this news before they boarded the ARC.

01:19:09.700 --> 01:19:11.860
Now we can't do anything to call our labors back.

01:19:12.360 --> 01:19:16.060
Anyway, it proves Hoba did plan this terrible chaos, and we've got to stop him.

01:19:16.280 --> 01:19:17.580
So let him finish off the mission.

01:19:17.980 --> 01:19:18.800
But hold on a minute.

01:19:19.460 --> 01:19:23.820
You said that any contact with the HOS would mean that the virus would pass on immediately.

01:19:24.240 --> 01:19:26.260
They'll be relying on the ARC computer.

01:19:26.420 --> 01:19:28.420
That surely had contact with the HO system.

01:19:29.520 --> 01:19:30.000
Oh!

01:19:32.080 --> 01:19:35.790
- Level D, Block 5, 30 seconds to purge.

01:19:35.790 --> 01:19:38.720
30 seconds to purge.

01:19:38.720 --> 01:19:42.840
All personnel evacuate immediately.

01:19:42.840 --> 01:19:46.930
Level D, Block 5, all personnel evacuate immediately.

01:20:01.690 --> 01:20:03.480
- Block D5 purged.

01:20:03.480 --> 01:20:05.900
Alphonse is heading towards D7.

01:20:05.900 --> 01:20:07.120
Okay, next one.

01:20:07.120 --> 01:20:08.400
Let's have the code for D7.

01:20:08.400 --> 01:20:10.840
- FPD 70460.

01:20:10.840 --> 01:20:12.200
Once Noah's gone up a level,

01:20:12.200 --> 01:20:15.400
there's no reason not to drop the external floors under her.

01:20:15.400 --> 01:20:17.340
- If we drop too many floors at once,

01:20:17.340 --> 01:20:20.070
we might throw the entire structure off balance.

01:20:20.070 --> 01:20:23.130
Don't worry, if we simply purge the exposed windbreaks,

01:20:23.130 --> 01:20:25.810
we should be able to slow up the resonance effect.

01:20:25.810 --> 01:20:28.540
What's the wind speed?

01:20:28.540 --> 01:20:30.000
- 35 meters per second.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:37.220
rising to 36 per second purge d7 right level d block seven commencing purge level d block seven

01:20:37.220 --> 01:20:38.900
commencing purge

01:21:37.770 --> 01:21:39.530
Right, what's the code for E2?

01:21:40.240 --> 01:21:43.530
Oh, Asuma, it's begun!

01:21:43.530 --> 01:21:45.810
D-level at 3, 5, and 7!

01:21:45.810 --> 01:21:47.340
C-level 2!

01:21:47.340 --> 01:21:48.760
Labor activity everywhere!

01:21:48.760 --> 01:21:50.010
Look!

01:21:50.010 --> 01:21:51.060
Why?

01:21:51.060 --> 01:21:53.520
The wind speed isn't up to 40 yet!

01:21:53.520 --> 01:21:55.760
Maybe the simulation wasn't accurate.

01:21:55.760 --> 01:21:59.000
Or else, the purge has created extra resonance!

01:22:01.950 --> 01:22:04.070
get me, you bastards! Come and try

01:22:04.070 --> 01:22:06.210
your luck! What's going on,

01:22:06.270 --> 01:22:08.170
Harumi? Rampaging labors on this

01:22:08.170 --> 01:22:10.290
level coming across the bridge. There's plenty

01:22:10.290 --> 01:22:12.230
of them. Oda's fighting them off. Where's

01:22:12.230 --> 01:22:14.150
Kanaka? She said she needed to find

01:22:14.150 --> 01:22:16.070
a weapon and left us here. What do we

01:22:16.070 --> 01:22:17.500
do now? Where is she?

01:22:18.340 --> 01:22:20.850
What's she doing? Power on.

01:22:22.180 --> 01:22:23.400
All systems normal.

01:22:24.730 --> 01:22:26.550
Type Zero standing by.

01:22:29.680 --> 01:22:30.000
Kanaka!

01:22:30.730 --> 01:22:31.890
Type 0 is too dangerous.

01:22:32.310 --> 01:22:34.310
Its protective system may have rejected the virus.

01:22:34.630 --> 01:22:37.030
I realize it's a gamble, but we've got to take the risk.

01:22:37.370 --> 01:22:38.670
But it might take you over.

01:22:39.170 --> 01:22:41.300
If we leave it, it might activate anyway.

01:22:41.840 --> 01:22:44.700
Even Ota can't stand up against all the labors he's trying to fight alone.

01:22:45.040 --> 01:22:46.700
But with the Type 0, I can go in and help.

01:22:46.700 --> 01:22:48.080
So over and out.

01:23:08.160 --> 01:23:09.850
Activate it sooner than expected.

01:23:09.850 --> 01:23:10.760
Don't waste time.

01:23:10.760 --> 01:23:12.730
Rearm Alphonse and take the shortest route

01:23:12.730 --> 01:23:13.790
to the sub-control route.

01:23:13.790 --> 01:23:14.630
Hurry.

01:23:14.630 --> 01:23:15.720
- Roger, will do.

01:25:12.090 --> 01:25:16.290
The wind speed's hit 40, Asuma! We can't afford to delay the final purge any longer!

01:25:16.290 --> 01:25:18.050
Come in, Noah! Come in!

01:25:18.050 --> 01:25:24.900
I've got no time for that now! We need to know if there's anybody there!

01:25:35.050 --> 01:25:39.650
No response the main computer must have been infected as well

01:25:44.960 --> 01:25:52.130
There are more and more labors coming at us too many to count and if they attack we can't hold them all off

01:25:52.450 --> 01:25:54.670
Help us get the purge underway now

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:02.470
The computer's out, but there must be some other way.

01:26:02.470 --> 01:26:11.550
There's gotta be an emergency backup system that's independent of the computer.

01:26:11.550 --> 01:26:12.390
Yeah.

01:26:12.390 --> 01:26:17.600
How do we get into the backup through all this chaos?

01:26:17.600 --> 01:26:19.110
Just hurry up!

01:26:19.110 --> 01:26:27.300
It's located just under the sub-control room.

01:26:27.300 --> 01:26:30.000
The top of the main shaft right by Noah, obviously.

01:26:30.060 --> 01:26:32.160
our reward for going to rescue anybody in that

01:26:32.160 --> 01:26:34.140
room. Now we've got access to the backup,

01:26:34.480 --> 01:26:36.140
we'll be able to complete the purge.

01:26:38.880 --> 01:26:39.360
Bastard!

01:26:39.360 --> 01:26:40.240
Do it!

01:27:10.620 --> 01:27:11.270
Zero!

01:27:48.040 --> 01:28:00.000
percussion revolver that you'll find in the compartment on the main drum idea what

01:28:00.280 --> 01:28:05.160
to the structures balance, you'll have 30 seconds to get yourself back inside Alphonse.

01:28:05.160 --> 01:28:09.600
He'll protect you. Activate now, Noah!

01:28:09.600 --> 01:28:19.880
Roger! Purging! Activate it!

01:28:39.820 --> 01:28:40.440
Yuka!

01:30:46.280 --> 01:30:46.960
*sigh*

01:31:41.200 --> 01:31:43.830
I think I've had just about enough, huh?

01:32:20.250 --> 01:32:21.510
Get out of there, Noah, quick.

01:32:21.930 --> 01:32:23.260
You can't defeat a Type Zero.

01:32:25.180 --> 01:32:28.060
No use.

01:32:28.450 --> 01:32:30.000
I've already taken it out, but the thing...

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.400
still running. I think the virus has gotten into the SRAM and that's

01:32:34.400 --> 01:32:39.540
sustaining it. Where's the SRAM? Back of the neck, the same as the 98.
